gpkg compress oracle case: long-basename

Isolates the container GNU switch at len(basename) >= 154 (gpkg.py:1007-1008):
a 154-character basename makes the container (not the inner tars) GNU even
though a 154-byte prefix would still fit USTAR's 155-byte prefix field.  If
the native writer used USTAR here, the `container.member ... fmt=GNU pre=L`
lines become fmt=USTAR pre=-.  Real behaviour worth knowing: only the members
written by container.addfile (gpkg-1, Manifest) become GNU + `L` records;
metadata.tar.<ext> and image.tar.<ext> are headed by tar_stream_writer with
the metadata (USTAR) / image format, and a 154-byte prefix still fits the
USTAR prefix field, so they stay USTAR without `L`.  Pair: basename-153 (one byte shorter, USTAR).
zstd only.

Run exactly as bin/ebuild-pyhelper runs gpkg-helper.py:
  /usr/bin/python <checkout>/bin/gpkg-helper.py compress <basename> <out> <metadata_dir> <image_dir>
with PYTHONPATH=<checkout>/lib, PORTAGE_BIN_PATH=<checkout>/bin, PORTAGE_PYM_PATH=<checkout>/lib,
PORTAGE_PYTHON=/usr/bin/python, under `env -i`, with a hermetic empty make.conf
(PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT=<scratch>/cfg); every setting real reads from portage.settings is
pinned in <comp>/env.  basename: lbxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx-1.0-1 (154 chars).
Inputs: image.manifest (this dir) materialised by ../materialise.py; metadata = ../metadata/
(25 build-info files of a real porttest build, see ../README.md).

